WEBVTT

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:08.580
~One Year Later~

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.080
<i>Hatori Yoshiyuki, 29 years old.</i>

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:18.160
<i>The second editor-in-chief of Emerald department at
Marukawa Publishing.</i>

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.950
<i>I'd at least like to produce work worthy of my title...</i>

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:34.420
But working overtime everyday really tires me out.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.020
<i>Disregarding other people's fatigue,</i>

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:04.120
<i>this guy taking over my bed is Yoshino Chiaki.</i>

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.050
<i>He's my childhood friend of 29 years and the mangaka
I'm in charge of.</i>

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.250
Are these rice balls?

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.340
<i>Though I have a bad feeling about this,</i>

00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:51.600
<i>atleast he made them for me.</i>

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.100
<i>How did he manage to make them taste like that?</i>

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:17.810
<i>Have some courtesy, will you?</i>

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:20.140
<i>Whose bed do you think this is?</i>

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:31.400
That's way too cold.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.420
<i>We've been going out for an year.</i>

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:54.080
<i>No matter what they say, the one who falls in love first loses.</i>

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.140
Goodnight.

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:06.670
Sekai-ichi Hatsukoi

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:10.980
Good morning. Are you awake?

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.040
If you are then go wash your face and brush your teeth.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.060
I'm making coffee.

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:27.520
Somehow, I dreamed about being crushed
by a giant pickle stone.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:33.200
<i>That pickle stone is supposed to be me, is it?</i>

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:38.560
Isn't your bad sleep quality because of your irregular
sleeping habits?

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.730
I slept pretty early yesterday.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.040
You have irregular sleeping habit too.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:45.440
What?

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:46.580
Nothing.

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.460
Anyway, how's the characterization of the new series
coming along?

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:54.210
Don't talk about work first thing in the morning.

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:57.280
If you take too long then you're just digging your own grave.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.120
You understand, don't you?

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.870
I understand!

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:04.880
I have to design new characters that don't overlap with
the ones I already have so far.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:06.230
It's worrying me.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.740
What about the ones you drew the other day?

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:14.080
Yeah... but I still can't come up with a good male lead yet.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.890
When can you come up with one then?

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:16.900
Who knows...

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:20.230
Maybe today, maybe tomorrow...

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.680
Day after tomorrow, or the day after that...

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:25.650
What do you call the day after that?

00:04:29.550 --> 00:04:33.420
What's wrong?! It's just been in my head for a bit.

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.060
How about this for the character?

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:54.990
It's not bad but doesn't he seem a bit plain?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:57.950
Can't be helped since you're the model.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.710
But that's why if feels different from all the characters
till now, right?

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:06.430
Got it.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.810
For now I'll show Takano-san during the break.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:13.410
When you're done with the character plan, fax it to the
editorial department.

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.560
Roger!

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:16.250
I'll go wash my face.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.020
Brush your teeth too.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.620
I got it already! Are you my mom or something?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.840
Who could it be at this time?

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:28.430
Maybe Yuu?

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.910
Gah! It's from my mom!

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.360
You won't answer?

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.430
It'll be bad if I don't, right?

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:43.260
If it's your mom, she'll just call again if you don't answer it now.

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.020
That's true...

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.430
I hope she doesn't nag...

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:51.490
Hello?

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.080
Chiaki! Why didn't you answer right away?

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.040
Where are you right now?

00:05:57.140 --> 00:05:58.210
Tori's place.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.720
It's okay, I'm not causing him any trouble.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:05.310
<i>You're causing plenty of trouble.</i>

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.270
Veggies? Don't bother!

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:11.270
I wouldn't cook even if you gave them to me.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.750
Anyway, just come visit once in a while! Understand?

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:15.810
Ehh...!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.530
See ya.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.620
Ah, Mom! Give me the phone.

00:06:19.070 --> 00:06:20.680
Hello, Onii-chan, you know-

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.600
Yes, enough! I got it! Bye!

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:26.610
Geez! It'll be all be good if I just go, isn't it?

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:29.940
They're worried since you hardly ever go home.

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.460
Worried!? I'm almost 29!

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.690
Anyway, do you have any right to say that to me?

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.500
I do go home once in a while.

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:41.560
Anyway, I'm just a roaming son!

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:45.570
If you know that, at least call them once in a while.

00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:48.370
If I feel like it.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:49.890
Oh yeah,

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.830
even if I keep the veggies at my house, they'd just rot.

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:54.190
Is it okay if I bring them here?

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.570
That's fine but...

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.740
I'm going home today and staying the night,

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.070
so I won't be here tonight.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:01.990
Huh?

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:03.580
Why?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.740
My parents are on vacation,

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:08.740
so they asked me to take care of the tropical pet fish.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:11.270
What? Then let's go together!

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.910
Great! If you're with me, I get scolded less!

00:07:15.470 --> 00:07:17.360
And then, I'll sleep at your place!

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.330
At our place, Mom and little sis just won't shut up...

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:22.930
I don't mind.

00:07:23.020 --> 00:07:24.370
Yes! It's decided then!

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:27.710
Oh! I feel hungry now that I'm relaxed.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.470
What's for breakfast today?

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.740
The rice from the rice balls you made.

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:32.940
Ehh!!

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:38.740
You, were you just making me eat what you
didn't want to yourself?

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.490
I ate half of it!

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:43.970
The rest was your share.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:46.700
<i>Are you a primary school kid?</i>

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.860
<i>I can understand why your Mom and others nag you.</i>

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:58.270
Wow, I'm amazed! How could something so bad become edible?

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:04.710
After adding heaps of tomato sauce and cooking with chopped
vegetables, most things become okay.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.920
But why did it taste so bad?

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.550
I didn't do anything weird.

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:16.450
Did you wash the rice properly before cooking?

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.020
No, just chucked it in the cooker.

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.100
Did you add the right amount of water?

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:23.910
Might have been a bit too less.

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:27.390
How much salt did you add when rolling the rice balls?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.070
Enough to cover both my hands.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.300
That way, there's less left over, right?

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.300
Just as I thought.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.450
Our rice isn't non-wash

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.550
and you only need a pinch of salt for rice balls.

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.640
Really!?

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.180
I see...

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:46.080
And I had finally decided to challenge cooking too.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.520
I get it, I'll give up.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.240
I thought I had to at least learn the basics.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.850
But Tori's cooking is more delicious.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:57.430
I've decided to just eat.

00:08:57.830 --> 00:08:58.730
I've repented.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.980
Is that called repenting?

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:04.310
What's wrong? Anyway, we'll always be together.

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.170
<i>Yoshino... you don't understand, do you?</i>

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:14.720
<i>Even if they are thoughtless to you...</i>

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:17.670
<i>...your unconscious words are a sin.</i>

00:09:19.550 --> 00:09:20.070
Nothing.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:26.280
Well taste aside, for you to cook for me, I'm grateful for that.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.250
Thanks.

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:30.600
Wh-Why so serious?

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.210
I'm just expressing my gratitude.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.080
Do you have a problem with that?

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:38.140
It's not like that but... it's just...

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.320
Yoshino

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:51.760
Hey Tori, it is okay if we go to your home first?

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.400
What are you saying? You're Mom's waiting, isn't she?

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:57.750
Alright, fine!

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.490
Then, let's get this over with!

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:07.350
I'm ba-

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:08.590
Welcome back.

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.150
You've finally come.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:14.600
Mom!? Wh-Wh-Why were you waiting there!?

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:16.720
I heard you guys talking.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.360
It's been a while, Yoshiyuki-kun.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:23.220
You've become more handsome in the time I haven't seen you.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.040
Thank you.

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.920
Haven't visited in a long time.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:30.490
Your mother was worried that you seem quite busy with work.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.090
Chiaki isn't causing any trouble, is he?

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:36.020
No. He's working pretty hard.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:39.340
Right now, he brings in the bacon for the company.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:43.900
Really? If Yoshiyuki-kun is saying so then I feel a bit better.

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:47.960
Oh dear, why are we standing here? Come in!

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:50.480
Someone gave us a watermelon!

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:52.130
Oh no, I'll be going now.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.070
Me too!

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:54.650
No need to be so polite.

00:10:54.940 --> 00:10:56.510
Don't you run away, Chiaki!

00:11:00.050 --> 00:11:01.460
Welcome back, Onii-chan!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:03.460
You're finally back!

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:05.350
I'm back, Chinatsu.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:08.450
Yoshiyuki-kun!?

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.220
Oh no, Onii-chan! You should have told me that you
were bringing him!

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:13.100
Why?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:16.730
No reason! Um, Yoshiyuki-kun, come in.

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:19.980
What's with her?

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.720
Here, please eat up!

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:37.490
Yes.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.920
This feels nostalgic.

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:42.090
I never buy watermelons by myself.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.520
Right?

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:46.800
It's so big that we can't finish it by ourselves,

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.880
so it's great you two dropped by.

00:11:50.050 --> 00:11:52.460
Aren't you the one who told us to come?

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:54.080
Chiaki...

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:56.760
It's nothing!

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.150
Oh, Chinatsu.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.600
Do you want some watermelon?

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:07.190
No. I'm alright.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:11.350
Oh! Mom! You haven't made any tea!

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:13.090
Yoshiyuki-kun, is barley tea okay?

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:15.460
It's fine, you don't have to worry so much.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:17.650
It's okay. I want some too.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.690
By the way, I heard Yoshiyuki-kun is now the second-in-chief?

00:12:24.350 --> 00:12:26.060
That's wonderful!

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:27.320
Not at all.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:31.890
I heard from your mom that you're always busy.

00:12:32.340 --> 00:12:35.020
Hey, Chiaki, what about you?

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:37.340
Are you busy right now too?

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:41.170
I don't have any deadlines this month, so I'm pretty relaxed.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:45.090
Actually, if I did have a deadline, I wouldn't be here
eating watermelons.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.580
What do you do at home with all that spare time?

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:50.030
Reading manga and scribbling.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.580
That's the same as always then!

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.950
Stop doing that all day and go find a nice girl

00:12:56.140 --> 00:12:58.450
and put your mother's heart at ease.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:00.630
E-Even if you say that...

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.830
Where am I supposed to find one...?

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.510
My work is isolated at home.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:08.560
Go to parties or pick up girls off the street or something.

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:11.010
Oh, but not someone from the same profession.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.770
The working hours are too irregular.

00:13:14.670 --> 00:13:15.840
Y-Yeah.

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:21.160
If she's not a girl who can take care of you,
then I can't die in peace.

00:13:21.260 --> 00:13:23.870
Why are you saying such unlucky things!?

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:26.810
You look like you'll live way longer than me.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:28.120
Oh, is that so?

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.910
Anyway, what about you, Yoshiyuki-kun?

00:13:36.930 --> 00:13:38.080
Do you have a girlfriend?

00:13:38.220 --> 00:13:40.860
It's a good time to start thinking about marriage.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.020
I'm so busy with work that it's impossible.

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:47.090
Oh dear, you too?

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.020
Such a waste, you're such a nice boy too!

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:54.990
Ahh, if only I had a son like you.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:58.070
Oh, that's right. What do you think of Chinatsu?

00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:02.840
What's wrong? You two have such terrible table manners!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:04.420
Stop it, Mom!

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:08.080
If you say something like that, it's awkward for Yoshiyuki-kun!

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.610
Oh, it that so?

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.230
Oh... Or are you dating someone?

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:15.680
D-Don't butt into my business!

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:19.820
What do you mean butt in? I'm worried about you!

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:21.880
Isn't that so, Yoshiyuki-kun?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.440
Ah, yes.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:28.680
But Chitasu-chan has grown to be very pretty in the time
I haven't seen her.

00:14:29.110 --> 00:14:31.240
She deserves someone better than me.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:33.850
Oh my... really?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:35.970
Did you hear that, Chinatsu?

00:14:36.780 --> 00:14:37.630
Enough!

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:39.830
You stop too, Yoshiyuki-kun!

00:14:40.160 --> 00:14:40.810
Sorry.

00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:42.810
Chinatsu?

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:46.020
I wonder what's wrong...

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.860
Tori... lend me the key to your house.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:49.700
What?

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.140
The fish need to be fed, don't they?

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.980
Wait, the vegetables!

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:01.540
Seriously, that kid's still so restless.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:12.500
Yoshino!

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.380
Sorry.

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:40.640
Mom said some weird stuff.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:42.210
Not really.

00:15:42.580 --> 00:15:43.900
It was only normal, wasn't it?

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.960
About Chinatsu too...

00:15:46.680 --> 00:15:47.860
...that is...

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.450
...Sorry...

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.040
About what?

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:58.930
No... just that... it's not your fault that she got angry... that is...

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:01.610
Could it be, you're...

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.270
Wh-What?

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:06.560
Can't be...

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:08.740
Are you jealous of Chinatsu-chan?

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:13.350
It-It's not like that! That's not it...

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:18.690
How should I say this... that is... I just thought it was bothersome.

00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.630
And Chinatsu is a girl too...

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:24.550
She'd be perfect for you...

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:27.140
For two guys to be together...

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.720
And you are an only child too...

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:36.140
True, it's not easy for two men to tell their family they're dating.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.760
But I've thrown away those worries long ago.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:45.600
Of course, I feel sorry for your mom.

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:46.980
But in return,

00:16:47.590 --> 00:16:50.040
I'll keep looking only at you my whole life.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:54.020
And also,

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:58.040
if I had to give up on you just for something like this,

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.600
would I one-sidedly love you for 28 years?

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:06.020
But, I'm glad.

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.710
A-About what?

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:12.850
It seems like you're starting to care about me a little.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:16.260
Th-That's not...

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:46.640
Wow! With your cooking skills, I can live with you forever!

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.860
Yeah yeah, just go do your work.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.200
Yes, yes.

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.820
Hand in your character plan before next week.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.260
Okay, I got it already. It's fine as long I do it right?

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.520
Here, Hatori. Fax for you.

00:18:27.910 --> 00:18:29.370
Oh, thanks.

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:40.500
Takano-san.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:43.660
It's the character plan for Yoshikawa-sensei's new work.

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:45.660
Could you check it please?

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:53.040
It's pretty good. It has a different feel from the
previous characters.

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:54.950
It will be popular with readers too.

00:18:55.680 --> 00:18:56.810
I see.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:18:59.490
Is anything bothering you?

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:02.350
Oh, no. Nothing like that.

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:05.330
I see. I'm counting on you to meet the deadline.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:09.810
Sensei is the type to lose track of days if you leave him be.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:10.920
Yes.

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:18.950
Hello?

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:21.390
It's Hatori from Marukawa Publishing.

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.910
Ah, Tori, did you see the character plan?

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.300
Yeah, it's good.

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:27.460
Takano-san also gave his okay.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.790
But, there's one thing I wanted to ask.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:33.170
What happened to the character you came up with before?

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:35.620
I can't see it on the character plan.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.110
Um, Yoshino?

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:41.900
I gave up on that.

00:19:42.000 --> 00:19:42.670
Gave up?

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:46.420
How should I put it... it's hard to draw.

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:48.030
What's hard to draw?

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:51.640
I mean... it's..

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.120
...That is...

00:19:53.470 --> 00:19:54.150
What?

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:55.640
I can't hear you.

00:19:55.820 --> 00:19:58.130
I mean the love scenes with the heroine!

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.990
Why do I have to draw the love scenes with you in it!?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.520
<i>He's the one who drew it in the first place.</i>

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:08.800
<i>What's he on about?</i>

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:17.090
Hey, Hatori.

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.170
What are you grinning about?

00:20:20.300 --> 00:20:21.260
It's creepy.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:24.870
Sorry.
